    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11077" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏphes</span></b> , ētis,
		or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏphen</span></b> ,
			ēnis (acc. Copheta or Cophen),
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river, a tributary of the Indus</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> Form Cophes, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 17,
				21, § 62</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 20, 23, §
			78</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			Form Cophen, <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 7, 1</span></i>.</div>
